ATTRIBUTION CORRECTION.

This commit's message describes the consensus convergence result (D0070), but a
concurrent 'git add -A' of mine swept in an in-flight agent's BPMD work that has
nothing to do with consensus:

    scripts/bpmd_run.py          (1026 lines) - the BPMD execution driver
    tests/test_bpmd_run.py        (316 lines) - its 22 tests
    shared/gromacs_explicit.py      (52 lines) - plumed_kernel() resolution
    scripts/setup_envs.sh           (26 lines) - build_plumed

Those belong to the BPMD driver work whose own record is 23f80ae. History was not
rewritten because another worker was active in the tree at the time.

The lesson is mine: 'git add -A' in a shared working tree stages whatever anyone
else has in flight, and a commit message that describes only my own change then
misattributes theirs. Stage explicitly when other work may be running.
